# Restless Vents played on turn 3 enters tapped, and Frantic Search untaps it. Bot1 then animates it with three sources, so it is an
# untapped creature, but it has not been under Bot1's control continuously since the turn began, so it cannot attack (CR 302.6, 508.1a):
# the attack is refused beside the Elvish Mystic, which attacks. On turn 5 the same animation lets the same land attack (the positive
# control) and Bot1's hand is empty, so there is no loot to answer; it deals 2 to Bot2 after the Mystic's 1 (20 - 1 - 2 = 17).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Elvish Mystic
Frantic Search
Restless Vents
Plains x3
Plains x10
[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Restless Vents.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Frantic Search.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Plains; Plains)
Bot1.Choose(Restless Vents; Island)
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Restless Vents.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Restless Vents.Activate(Ability: Until end of turn)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Restless Vents.Types = Land; Creature
? Bot1.Battlefield.Restless Vents.Tapped = false
! Bot1.Attack(Restless Vents > Bot2)
Bot1.Attack(Elvish Mystic > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Restless Vents.Activate(Ability: Until end of turn)
Bot1.Attack(Restless Vents > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 17

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
